id: GTTxCore
name: ᝯㄝₓ Core
metadata:
  description: "The shared half of the ᝯㄝₓ plugins, and the home for the things that belong to none of them.\n\nInstall this alongside any other ᝯㄝₓ plugin. They each declare it as a dependency, so Stash installs it with them and loads it first. What it holds is the code they all used to carry a copy of: the hover card that opens on an entity's name, the tooltip on a tag, the mark beside a setting that names a custom field, the red Reload UI button, and the rules that decide where a plugin's button lands in one of Stash's own rows and in what order when two plugins want the same row.\n\nScene Tagger duration warning: Stash's tagger prints \"Duration off by at least Ns\" in the same weight and colour as everything beside it, and it is the one line on that card that says whether a match is the right file. Turn this on and it is emphasised - larger, capitalised and red past five seconds, amber above one - and left exactly as Stash wrote it below that. It is off by default, because it changes a page this plugin does not own, and it changes nothing but the styling: no result is hidden, reordered or acted on.\n\nRight-click Paste: the Tags, Performers and Groups boxes offer no Paste in the browser's context menu, because the text input inside them is sized to what has been typed and a right-click with nothing typed lands beside it rather than on it. Turn this on and the input fills the rest of the row, so the browser offers its own Paste; the paste takes the same path Ctrl+V already does. Off by default.\n\nOpen Links in the Same Tab: the dialogs, listings and hover cards these plugins draw name entities as links, and every one of them opens a new tab so the dialog you are reading stays open behind it. Turn this on and they all open in the tab you are already in, the way Stash's own links do. It reaches every plugin at once and takes effect on the next link drawn. Off by default, which is a new tab.\n\nCounts on headings: the word Tags above a tag list says nothing about how long the list is. Turn Show Counts on Headings on and it reads Tags (12) - Stash's own word with the count after it - on the details view and the edit form of every scene, image, gallery, performer, studio, group and tag, and so do Performers (3) and Custom Fields (5) wherever an entity has them, all counted off what the page shows. Off by default, because it changes a page this plugin does not own; nothing is read from your library for it.\n\nDev Mods: three switches for working on these plugins rather than for using them. Debug mode turns on the console channel that says why each injected control is shown or hidden; Layout edit mode outlines every control these plugins have added to Stash's chrome and labels it with the plugin that put it there; Stale UI demo makes the red Reload UI button appear without waiting for a real version mismatch. All three are off by default, none of them writes anything, and none is meant to be left on.\n\nUndo History: what the ᝯㄝₓ plugins write, and what you save in Stash's own pages in this browser, is kept in this browser so it can be undone later - from Settings - Tasks, Undo History..., or the ↶ button in Stash's top bar. Ticked changes are checked against what your library holds now and listed before anything is written, and a change is undone only while its field still holds what was written, so a later edit is never overwritten. An undo is itself recorded, so it can be undone in turn - or, if you tick that, taken out of the history together with what it undid, so the history goes back to a point. Runs you have no use for, test runs say, can be deleted from the history without touching your library. The history can be saved to a file and brought back, and Back Up and Export takes a database backup and saves the history with it. Edits made in another browser, by Stash's own tasks or by scripts are not recorded. A deleted tag, performer, studio, group or scene, and a tag merge, are put back under a new id.\n\nNothing else here writes to your library. If you uninstall it, every other ᝯㄝₓ plugin says so in its own settings group rather than failing quietly.\n\nRequires Stash 0.31.0 or newer."
